      "content": "# Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide\n\n## Introduction\nWelcome to the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor quick-start guide. This guide will help you set up, calibrate, and safely operate the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor.\n\n## Power Requirements\nThe Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor operates on 5V DC power supplied via USB-C. Ensure the power source meets these requirements to avoid damage to the sensor.\n\n## Setup\n1. Connect the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor to the Nexus Hub.\n2. Run the 'nexus-sync' command via terminal.\n3. Wait for the green LED to blink, indicating successful synchronization.\n\n## Calibration\n1. Hold the sensor 10cm from a flat surface.\n2. Press the 'Calibrate' button for 3 seconds.\n3. The sensor will automatically calibrate itself.\n\n## Safety\n1. Do not submerge the sensor in liquid.\n2. Do not exceed 5V power supply.\n3. Avoid high-intensity UV during calibration.\n\n## LED Status\n- Solid Green: The sensor is active.\n- Blinking Green: The sensor is syncing.\n- Red: The sensor has an error or no power.\n\n## Mounting\nMounting the Nexus",
